From cab5f570ca2535ffd5e61e544d815649e9f5bb75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:59:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Warn when Unleashed connects to an upstream app-server

Keep the server initialization version aligned with the Unleashed package's
numeric vendor build or dev suffix. Warn branded clients when a connected
server reports an upstream version without vendor metadata. Preserve existing
settings, connection deduplication, and local update guidance.

Base: openai/codex rust-v0.160.0 a956835d020762cb2b570053af06f643a11c0ecc.
Client branding is supplied by add-branding-and-build-metadata.patch.

RED: just test -p codex-login --lib -E 'test(user_agent_identifies_unleashed_server)'
failed on the upstream user agent without vendor identity.
RED: just test -p codex-tui --lib -E 'test(unleashed_client_warns) | test(unleashed_openai_server_warning)'
failed both tests because the OpenAI app-server warning was absent.
GREEN: just test -p codex-app-server -p codex-login -p codex-app-server-client -p codex-tui --lib --test all -E '(package(codex-app-server) & test(initialize_uses_client_info_name_as_originator)) | (package(codex-login) & test(default_client)) | (package(codex-app-server-client) & test(remote_)) | (package(codex-tui) & (test(status::remote_connection) | test(server_version) | test(unleashed_)))'
37 tests passed with INSTA_UPDATE=no, including real process initialization,
WebSocket metadata preservation, provider selection, and rendering.
GREEN: just fmt-check passed.

A broader selector also ran unrelated analytics tests: 247 passed, two
remote plugin analytics cases timed out; pristine-baseline comparison remains
an integration check, not a claimed passing result.
